  <div class="prose"><p>The United States Research Software Engineer Association (<a href="https://us-rse.org/" target="_blank">us-rse.org</a>) is a community-driven effort bringing together people who write and contribute to research software within the United States. The organization aims to build a connective, supportive, and diverse community of individuals from universities, laboratories, knowledge institutes, companies, and other enterprises.</p></div>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>The User Experience (<a href="https://us-rse.org/wg/ux/" target="_blank">#wg-ux</a>) working group brings together individuals to share experiences and advocate for increased awareness and adoption of user experience (UX) methods in research software engineering. The group meets monthly on Zoom for open discussions and often facilitates other special events.</p>
    <p>This community's channel in the US-RSE Slack is an active space for discussion and collaboration. It is open to any US-RSE member (which is free).</p>
  </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section page-section" aria-labelledby="top-content">
  <div class="container split-layout">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">#wg-udx</p>
      <img src="https://cass.community/assets/images/cass-logo.png" alt="CASS logo" width="200" height="200">
    </div> 
  <div class="prose"><p>Consortium for the Advancement of Scientific Software (<a href="https://cass.community/" target="_blank">cass.community</a>) is a federation of member organizations committed to the stewardship and advancement of the current and future ecosystem of scientific computing software. Members support specific scientific communities or provide crosscutting capabilities for scientific software stewardship. Member organizations coordinate and cooperate through the Consortium to maximize benefit to the ecosystem as a whole.</p></div>
  <div class="prose"><p>The User/Developer Experience (<a href="https://cass.community/working-groups/user-developer-experience.html" target="_blank">UDX</a>) working group brings together groups and individuals interested in the science of scientific software development and use. The UDX WG organizes bi-monthly webinars to improve understanding of how users and developers interact with and experience scientific software.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

